- F-329 **A `Char`'s `asExprString` writes one text on both paths, which the parser reads back at every code point.** Walk's binding and the prelude's name `nativeHelpers/simpleChar.charToExprString` (P-163): `'\"'`, `'\\'`, the five escapes, the code alone for the other controls, U+201C, U+201D, U+2028, U+2029, the surrogates and past U+FFFF, else the character, a space and its code, `'é 00e9'`. The parser reads codes of four to six digits in either case (`parser/Literal.rats:460-466`). A character past U+FFFF written as itself does not parse (row 924). Test: `tests/NativeHelperFamilyCharWalk`, `compiler_tests/NativeHelperFamilyCharCompiled`, `tests/CharExprStringReadBack`; `tests/XXXCharLiteralSupplementary`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-char-expr-string/REPORT.md`, "Old against new: every code point in six forms".
