- F-32 **The compiled path cannot reuse walk's glue classes, the Java classes that 102 of the one library's 443 live native bindings still name.** A native binding is a library body `builtinPrimitive("…")`; its string names a glue class, which takes walk's boxed values, or a static helper of `nativeHelpers/`, over plain Java values, which both paths call (F-298; F-299 holds the 341 that name one). Matched against those helpers at `a1f8c4b8b`, before any binding moved, the 449 were: 154 whose operation the compiler's prelude already binds to a helper at the same owner and signature, so only the binding's string changes, to name that helper (P-58); 59 whose helper exists, but no binding names it under that name and signature, 23 of them under a name that the compiler's prelude gives to another helper, such as the 12 wrapping operators (row 348); 158 that need a new helper; and 78 that need more, 36 methods of native I/O objects and 42 with no compiled analogue. Of the 449, 29 are object `IntLiteral`'s (`FortressBuiltin.fss:486-563`), 4 among the 154 and 25 among the 158; none of them can move yet, since their helpers take and answer the compiled path's `IntLiteral`, which walk's values cannot be, and walk reaches no `IntLiteral` native while its numeral is an `Int` (P-76; row 578). `println` writes through `stdOut`, a plain Fortress `Writer` over `JavaBufferedWriter`, whose natives name `fileOps` helpers (F-330). MicroGPT's `nanoTime` names a helper (F-314); it also needs `getProgramArgsPrim`, which `System` calls as it loads; and `NativeArray`. The last two have no compiled analogue. The 42 with no analogue: `NativeArray` waits for the array decision on how a float vector's `double[]` store goes (P-85), and `Thread`, `Reflect` and `printTaskTrace` are off microGPT's path. Detail: `compile-ladder/climb-batch-27/RECORD.md`, "The count of the bindings"; `perf-probes/prelude/natives-shape.md` section 2; `coordinator/CLIMB-BATCH-23.md`, section 4, "The planner's probes", "On the new base" and "The count".
  from: compile-ladder/climb-batch-27/RECORD.md, "The count of the bindings"; from: reviews/batch-27-review.md, "6. The natives and the code generator after phase 4's fifth batch"; commit: a2f0b5cf2; note: climb batch 27's gather's count of the merged tree, comments struck: 340 of 441 strings and 101, so 341 of 443 and 102 by F-299's count; Writer and stdOut plain Fortress objects since rung W, c21780408 (Library/Writer.fss:17, :25; println at Library/FortressLibrary.fss:4646)

- F-299 **Walk loads a `builtinPrimitive` string that names a static helper of `nativeHelpers/` beside its glue classes, and 341 of the one library's 443 live bindings name one.** It builds P-58, "Every native binding is a ...", whose compiled half F-298 gives. The loader (`interpreter/glue/StaticNativeApp.java`) calls the overload whose Java types carry the declared types, `self` first, and raises a helper's `fortress.<Api>$<Name>` as the library's `<Name>`. It refuses at load a string that names no helper or fits none, and a declared type that no Java type carries, `self`'s among them, read from the declaring type. For `stringOps.typeName` and `equality.sEquiv` it runs walk's own operations instead, by the table of `interpreter/glue/NativeApp.java` (F-328). The library's own `FlatString`, identified by the component that declares it, carries `self` in a Java `String`; a program's own type named `FlatString` or `JavaString` carries none. A helper parameter declared `String` is refused at load, 'no Java type carries the declared type of parameter', since a Java `String` cannot carry a string that is not flat; one declared `FlatString` or `JavaString`, and a result declared `String`, are carried in a Java `String`. Its departures: a generic owner's dotted method is checked only where an instance is made (row 864); the declaring type is read, not the value's, so a program's object that extends a carried trait against its `comprises` clause passes the helper a value that no Java type carries (row 551); a glue class bound over `String` receives a non-flat string's type name, and so would a helper bound in a method of the trait `String`, as `self`; the library binds no helper there (row 846). The 341 by type: `ZZ32` 28 and `Int` 3, `ZZ64` 29 and `ZZ` 26 (F-306, F-327; their `CHOOSE` F-305, `REM` and `MOD` F-312, divisors F-314), `Float` 62 and the top-level `fromRawBits` (F-303, F-323), `RR32` 51 (F-310, its `asFloat` F-311), the `asFloat`s of `Long` and `BigNum` 2 (F-311), the small rest 8 (F-307), and `NN32` 30, `NN64` 27, `UnsignedLong` 3 and `Char` 40 (F-308, F-313, F-327), the top-level `nanoTime` (F-314) and `random` (F-323), `Object`'s `ilkName` and `SEQV` over `Any` (F-328), `JavaBufferedWriter`'s 7 (F-330), and the string family's 20: `FlatString`'s 13 methods; `natLineSeparator`; `match`; and `printThreadInfo`, `printWithThread`, `printlnWithThread`, `getEnvironment` and `getProperty`, each a native over `FlatString` beside an overload over `String` that flattens in a `typecase`; the other 102 name glue classes. The `fortress-repo` skill's `references/interpreter.md`, "Natives", gives the carriers and the messages. Test: `tests/NativeHelperBindingWalk.fss`, `NativeHelperRaiseWalk`, `ZZ32DivisionByZeroWalk`, `NativeHelperFamilyZZ32Walk`, `NativeHelperCarriedSelfFlatStringWalk`, `NativeHelperStringRopeWalk`, `compiler_tests/NativeHelperFamilyStringCompiled`, and the refusals `NativeHelperMisspeltWalk`, `NativeHelperMisfitWalk`, `NativeHelperUncarriedWalk`, `NativeHelperUncarriedSelf*Walk` and `NativeHelperNonFlatStringWalk`; the entries of the other families name their own tests. Detail: `compile-ladder/climb-batch-27/RECORD.md`, "The count of the bindings"; `compile-ladder/rung-natives-walk/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why"; `compile-ladder/rung-natives-self/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why"; `compile-ladder/rung-string-natives/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why".
